From: Roki Buildroot <build@roki.local>
Subject: [PATCH] rpi: export the Unicam Bayer frame sequence

Expose the V4L2 sequence of the Bayer buffer that feeds the VC4 ISP as
request metadata. This preserves the hardware camera sequence without
requiring applications to configure a RAW output stream.

---
 src/libcamera/control_ids_rpi.yaml       | 14 ++++++++++++++
 src/libcamera/pipeline/rpi/vc4/vc4.cpp |  4 ++++
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/control_ids_rpi.yaml b/src/libcamera/control_ids_rpi.yaml
index 9d0f300..2222507 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/control_ids_rpi.yaml
+++ b/src/libcamera/control_ids_rpi.yaml
@@ -308,4 +308,18 @@ controls:
         This control returns performance metrics for the CNN processing stage.
         Two values are returned in this span, the runtime of the CNN/DNN stage
         and the DSP stage in milliseconds.
+
+  - UnicamSequence:
+      type: int64_t
+      direction: out
+      description: |
+        The hardware frame sequence from the VC4 Unicam image buffer used
+        to produce this request. This is the V4L2 capture sequence, not the
+        request sequence or the ISP output buffer sequence. It is available
+        even when the application configures only processed output streams.
+
+        The underlying counter is unsigned 32-bit and may wrap. Its origin
+        is the start of Unicam streaming, not the first frame delivered to
+        the application; startup and dropped frames can leave gaps.
+        This metadata is only provided by the Raspberry Pi VC4 pipeline.
 ...
diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/rpi/vc4/vc4.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/rpi/vc4/vc4.cpp
index ac86a43..7cd0b83 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/rpi/vc4/vc4.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/rpi/vc4/vc4.cpp
@@ -984,6 +984,10 @@ void Vc4CameraData::tryRunPipeline()
 
 	fillRequestMetadata(bayerFrame.controls, request);
 
+	/* Keep the hardware input sequence paired with this request's ISP output. */
+	request->_d()->metadata().set(controls::rpi::UnicamSequence,
+				       static_cast<int64_t>(bayerFrame.buffer->metadata().sequence));
+
 	unsigned int bayer = unicam_[Unicam::Image].getBufferId(bayerFrame.buffer);
 
 	LOG(RPI, Debug) << "Signalling prepareIsp:"
-- 
2.51.0
